# From 0.1.6 each app carries its own LibreOffice settings, which until then
# were all in this package, so an older Write or Tables beside this one would
# be without its default format. apt then updates all of them together.
Breaks: wildos-write (<< 0.1.6~), wildos-tables (<< 0.1.6~)
Description: Wild OS Write, Tables and Slides, the parts all three share
 Documents, spreadsheets and presentations for Wild OS. Write, Tables and
 Slides are LibreOffice Writer, Calc and Impress with Wild OS start screens,
 ribbons and defaults: Word, Excel and PowerPoint files open with them and
 save back as .docx, .xlsx and .pptx unless asked otherwise. This package
 holds what they share; wildos-write, wildos-tables and wildos-slides are
 the apps, so each can be removed on its own.

Package: wildos-write
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 wildos-office (>= 0.1.6),
 libreoffice-writer,
Breaks: wildos-office (<< 0.1.4~)
Replaces: wildos-office (<< 0.1.4~)
Description: Wild OS Write
 Documents for Wild OS: LibreOffice Writer with the Wild OS start screen,
 ribbon and defaults. Word files open with it and save back as .docx.

Package: wildos-tables
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 wildos-office (>= 0.1.6),
 libreoffice-calc,
Breaks: wildos-office (<< 0.1.4~)
Replaces: wildos-office (<< 0.1.4~)
Description: Wild OS Tables
 Spreadsheets for Wild OS: LibreOffice Calc with the Wild OS start screen,
 ribbon and defaults. Excel files open with it and save back as .xlsx.

Package: wildos-slides
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
